5. Clinical trials: Once the optimized drug candidates have been identified, they can be tested in clinical trials to evaluate their efficacy and safety in human subjects. This is the final step in the process of developing a new treatment for skin diseases.

By following these steps, the principles of medicinal chemistry can be used to develop new treatments for skin diseases that are more effective and have fewer side effects.
