   \[
   f(x - \frac{\pi}{10}) = \sin \left( \omega x - \frac{\omega \pi}{10} + \varphi \right)
   \]  

2. **Symmetry about the origin:**  
   The new function is symmetric about the origin, which means \( f(x - \frac{\pi}{10}) = -f(x - \frac{\pi}{10}) \).  
   Substituting \( f(x - \frac{\pi}{10}) \):  
   \[
