Point $D$ is on side $AC$ of triangle $ABC$, where $\angle ABD=30^{\circ}$ and $\angle DBC=60^{\circ}$. Determine the measure of angle $BAD$ in degrees.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The angles in a triangle add up to $180^\circ$. Since $\angle ABD = 30^\circ$ and $\angle DBC = 60^\circ$, we have $\angle ABD + \angle DBC = 30^\circ + 60^\circ = 90^\circ$. Therefore, $\angle ABC = 90^\circ$.

The angles in a triangle add up to $180^\circ$, so $\angle BAD + \angle ABC + \angle BCA = 180^\circ$. Substituting $\angle ABC = 90^\circ$, we get $\angle BAD + 90^\circ + \angle BCA = 180^\circ$. Therefore, $\angle BAD + \angle BCA = 90^\circ$.

Since $D$ is on $AC$, $\angle BAD + \angleBAD = \angleABC = 90^\circ$. Therefore, $\angle BAD = \frac{90^\circ}{2} = 45^\circ$.

The measure of angle $BAD$ is $\boxed{45^\circ}$.

</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

