After the first refill, the total number of seeds is $0.2 + 0.2 + 0.3 + 0.3 = 0.8$.  

The number of millet seeds remaining is $0.2 - 0.2 \times 0.3 = 0.14$.  

The number of non-millet seeds remaining is $0.3 - 0.3 \times 0.9 = 0.21$.  

The proportion of millet is $\frac{0.14}{0.8} = 0.175$.  

The proportion of millet increases with each refill, so the answer is $\boxed{D}$.

