In a process where hands are rubbed together, the friction force is \( F_{\text{fr}} \) and the mean relative velocity of one hand with respect to the other is \( v \). The room temperature is \( T \). Determine the entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) of this process.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{dU}{T},
\]
where \( U \) is the change in internal energy of the system.

For the rubbing of hands, the work done by the friction force \( F_{\text{fr}} \) is converted into heat, which increases the internal energy of the system (the two hands). The work done is:
\[
dW = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt,
\]
where \( dt \) is the time interval.

The change in internal energy is then:
\[
dU = dW = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt.
\]

Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{dU}{T} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt}{T} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}.
\]

Final answer: \(\boxed{\frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}}\)

</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

